            <ArticleTitle>Multivessel variant angina unresponsive to urapidil.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>439-43</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of variant angina complicated by recurrent sudden cardiac death. During coronary angiography a diffuse 3-vessel vasoconstriction was observed progressing to a more severe vasoconstriction in the mid LAD. Intracoronary administration of urapidil did not reverse the vasoconstriction of the LAD; instead an occlusive vasospasm occurred accompanied by marked ischaemia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
